KEY SEMANTICS
-------------
- Retry and recovery are opt-in: retry_safe/default False, only aj.echo/aj.health_check are True
- Cancellation is cooperative: EXECUTING -> CANCEL_REQUESTED (honest "not interrupted" message); non-running -> CANCELLED
- Import is conservative: validate first, refuse task-id conflicts, no deletion, dry-run, summaries rebuilt (derived)
- Operation leases are advisory and POSIX-first; expired lease does not authorize mutation
- Journal is append-only; stores only correlation metadata, never task payloads
- Idempotency key scoped to capability; duplicates return first task id
- Scheduler claims tasks atomically via lease acquisition; bounded concurrency
- Dependency checking (depends_on): blocked until all dependencies COMPLETED
- Lineage (parent_task_id/root_task_id): tree structure traversal

CORRELATION FLOW
----------------
task -> attempt -> audit -> memory -> logs -> journal -> receipts
All carry operation_id and attempt_id for cross-system tracing.

EXIT CODE MAP
-------------
0: OK (successful completion)
1: RETRY_UNSAFE (capability not retry-safe)
2: CONFLICT (lease held, task-id conflict on import)
3: RECOVERY_REQUIRED (capability not replay-safe)
4: CANCELLED (task was cancelled)
5: CONFIG_INVALID (bad configuration)
6: UNSAFE (retry of non-retry-safe capability)

